{
  "id": "COMPOUND:28862 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Dendocarbin K is shown to interact with SNU-387, which is a target of multiple compounds, including 10,22-Dihydroxy-7,7,18,18-tetramethyl-8,13,17-trioxapentacyclo[12.8.0.03,12.04,9.016,21]docosa-1(22),3(12),4(9),10,14,16(21),19-heptaen-2-one and 3-Bromo-4-(2,3-Dibromo-4,5-Dihydroxybenzyl)-5-Methoxymethylpyrocatecol. These compounds all target Phosphodiesterase 6C, suggesting a shared mechanism of action involving the enzyme. The evidence indicates that Dendocarbin K may inhibit Phosphodiesterase 6C through a common pathway, possibly by binding to and modulating the activity of the enzyme. The presence of multiple targets for SNU-387 and their subsequent targeting of Phosphodiesterase 6C suggests a potential role in the regulation of intracellular signaling pathways, possibly involving the breakdown of second messengers. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Dendocarbin K and Phosphodiesterase 6C, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific mode of action and therapeutic relevance.",
